  "title": "Sharp thresholds for graph properties",
  "description": "OpenAI's proofs (2026) of the Friedgut–Kalai conjectures: increasing graph properties of G(n,p) have threshold width O(log(1/ε)/(log n)²), and r-uniform hypergraph properties width O((log n)^(−r/(r−1))). The course develops biased Fourier analysis and hypercontractivity, restricts symmetric functions to the edges meeting a random block of vertices, and captures each Fourier support at one vertex.",
